  "expenditureUncertaintyLegend": "Uncertainty margin",
  "expenditureDisclaimer": "This estimate is calculated from your weight and food journal (same principle as TOTUM's adaptive calibration) — it is not a direct measurement, nor a reproduction of another app's proprietary algorithm. The more regularly you log your weight and meals, the tighter the uncertainty margin becomes.",
  "expenditureRecentEvolution": "Recent evolution",
  "expenditureInfoTooltip": "What is this number?",
  "expenditureInfoTitle": "Estimated energy expenditure",
  "expenditureInfoWhatItIs": "This number is a real ~20-day AVERAGE: from how your weight actually changed and the calories you actually logged over that window, TOTUM works out the calories it really took for you to get that result. Same principle as the adaptive calibration that refines your calorie target — shown here day by day, as a trend line.",
  "expenditureInfoVsToday": "This is NOT the same number as \"Base metabolism\" + \"Movement\" shown on the dashboard: those are a formula-based calculation for TODAY ONLY (age, weight, declared activity level + your movement today). The number here is a rolling empirical average over several weeks — the two can legitimately diverge, especially if your food journal isn't filled in every day.",
  "expenditureInfoCoverageWarning": "Be cautious with sparsely-covered windows (fewer than half the days logged): a partially logged day (a forgotten snack, an unlogged sauce or drink) makes your intake look lower than it really was, pulling this estimate down. The more consistently you log, the more reliable this number becomes.",
  "expenditureInfoAutoRefresh": "You don't need to do anything special: this number recalculates itself every time you open the app, using only your COMPLETED days — today's meals never count until the day is over (otherwise logging just breakfast in the morning would make the estimate crash for no real reason). The \"Confirm my goals\" button on your Profile only validates a deliberate setting change (weight, goal...), it never \"refreshes\" this calculation.",
  "expenditureInfoSubtitle": "30 seconds: where this number comes from, and why it can differ from your other numbers.",
  "expenditureInfoEquationTitle": "Your total burn: the TDEE",
  "expenditureInfoTdeeSpellOut": "TDEE, for Total Daily Energy Expenditure — your total energy burn over a day. It breaks down into 4 pieces, in very unequal proportions:",
  "expenditureInfoEquationBmr": "BMR — Base metabolism",
  "expenditureInfoEquationBmrDesc": "What your body burns at rest just to function: breathing, circulation, brain, organs. The biggest share, ~70% — very little room to move it on a daily basis.",
  "expenditureInfoEquationNeat": "NEAT — Daily movement",
  "expenditureInfoEquationNeatDesc": "Everything you burn moving around without it being \"exercise\": walking, taking the stairs, standing, fidgeting. Highly variable from person to person — ~15% on average.",
  "expenditureInfoNeatLeverBadge": "Your most powerful lever, for most people",
  "expenditureInfoEquationTef": "TEF — Thermic effect of food",
  "expenditureInfoEquationTefDesc": "The energy your body uses to digest what you eat — ~10%. Varies with what you eat: protein takes the most, fat the least.",
  "expenditureInfoEquationEat": "EAT — Voluntary exercise",
  "expenditureInfoEquationEatDesc": "Exercise in the strict sense — what you deliberately add to your day. The smallest share on average (~5%), but the one that grows fastest with training.",
  "expenditureInfoTdeeCaption": "Average breakdown for a moderately active adult — real proportions vary a lot from person to person.",
  "expenditureInfoMethodsTitle": "2 methods, combined",
  "expenditureInfoMethodFormulaTitle": "The formula",
  "expenditureInfoMethodFormulaDesc": "Age, weight, height, sex, declared activity level → a scientific starting estimate (Mifflin-St Jeor / Cunningham). This is what sets your daily target and the dashboard donut.",
  "expenditureInfoMethodCalibTitle": "The calibration",
  "expenditureInfoMethodCalibDesc": "YOUR actual weight + the calories YOU actually logged over ~20 days → your burn, worked out from your real results. This is THE number shown here, on this curve.",
  "expenditureInfoMethodsFooter": "Totum combines both: the formula acts as a starting point and safety floor, real calibration refines it as your data builds up.",
  "expenditureInfoBalanceTitle": "The principle, in one sentence",
  "expenditureInfoBalanceBody": "If your weight isn't moving while you eat X kcal/day, that means you're also burning roughly X kcal/day. If your weight drops or rises, Totum adjusts this number accordingly — that's the whole calculation, literally a balance.",
  "expenditureInfoLiveCompareTitle": "Your current number, in context",
  "expenditureInfoBelowBmr": "{estimate} kcal/day is below your theoretical base metabolism ({bmr} kcal/day) — physiologically unlikely to hold continuously. The most common cause: unlogged meals recently, not a real drop in your burn. Keep logging regularly so this number moves closer to reality.",
