  "jrnlRestaurantsInfoTitle": "Restaurants: an occasional detour, not a staple",
  "jrnlRestaurantsInfoP1": "These chains come from the USDA database (Foundation Foods/SR Legacy) and are mostly North American fast-food and family-dining chains — recipes and portions reflect the U.S. market.",
  "jrnlRestaurantsInfoP2": "An average fast-food chain meal provides about 1200 kcal and 2100 mg of sodium in a single meal — well above the guidelines for one meal (roughly 700 kcal, under 770 mg of sodium).",
  "jrnlRestaurantsInfoP3": "The U.S. Dietary Guidelines Advisory Committee places a reasonable share of \"discretionary\" calories at 5 to 15% of weekly intake for most adults. In practice, that's roughly 1 to 2 meals of this type per week — a single one can already represent most of that budget.",
  "jrnlRestaurantsInfoP4": "Beyond 3 meals of this type per week, the evidence broadly agrees that this drifts noticeably away from an eating pattern oriented toward health, longevity, vitality and performance. For a gentler detour, \"healthy\"/fast-casual chains (composed salads, bowls, poke...) remain an alternative worth considering.",
